<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table"><span id="S0.T1.7" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Table 1</span>: </span><span id="S0.T1.8" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">
<span id="S0.T1.8.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Average entropy change of attention maps (<math id="S0.T1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta\mathcal{H}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta\mathcal{H}</annotation></semantics></math>) across diffusion steps.</span>
We extract attention maps corresponding to the tokens “<span id="S0.T1.8.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">cat</span>” and “<span id="S0.T1.8.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">dog</span>” from the prompt “A photo of a dog sitting next to a cat”.
</span></figcaption>
</figure>
</section>
<section id="S1a" class="ltx_section">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_section"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_section">A </span>Experimental Detail</h2>

<div id="S1a.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S1a.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We used the RTX3090 graphic card for training and inference. For inference, we used DDIM scheduler <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib34" title="" class="ltx_ref">34</a>]</cite> with 50 steps and 7.5 classifier-free guidance weight <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib12" title="" class="ltx_ref">12</a>]</cite>. We use Stable Diffusion v2-1<span id="footnote1" class="ltx_note ltx_role_footnote"><sup class="ltx_note_mark">1</sup><span class="ltx_note_outer"><span class="ltx_note_content"><sup class="ltx_note_mark">1</sup>
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_note">1</span>
            
            
            
            
            
            
            
          <a href="https://huggingface.co/stabilityai/stable-diffusion-2-1" title="" class="ltx_ref ltx_url ltx_font_typewriter">https://huggingface.co/stabilityai/stable-diffusion-2-1</a></span></span></span> with 768x768 resolution as the pre-trained model.</p>
</div>
<div id="S1a.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S1a.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S1a.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Textual Inversion <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib6" title="" class="ltx_ref">6</a>]</cite>.</span>
We use the third-party implementation of huggingface <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib38" title="" class="ltx_ref">38</a>]</cite> for Textual Inversion. We train each setting with a learning rate of <math id="S1a.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="5\times 10^{-4}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>5</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">5\times 10^{-4}</annotation></semantics></math>, step size of 3000, and batch size of 4.</p>
</div>
<div id="S1a.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S1a.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S1a.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">DreamBooth <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib29" title="" class="ltx_ref">29</a>]</cite>.</span>
We use the third-party implementation of huggingface <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib38" title="" class="ltx_ref">38</a>]</cite> for Dreambooth. We train each setting with a learning rate of <math id="S1a.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1\times 10^{-5}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>5</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1\times 10^{-5}</annotation></semantics></math>, step size of <math id="S1a.p3.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="400\times" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>400</mn><mo lspace="0.222em">×</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">400\times</annotation></semantics></math> number of subjects, and batch size of 1. Prior preservation loss was used, and a loss weight of 1 was used. 200 class images were used for prior preservation loss.</p>
</div>
<div id="S1a.p4" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S1a.p4.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S1a.p4.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Custom Diffusion <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib17" title="" class="ltx_ref">17</a>]</cite>.</span>
We use the official implementation of custom diffusion<span id="footnote2" class="ltx_note ltx_role_footnote"><sup class="ltx_note_mark">2</sup><span class="ltx_note_outer"><span class="ltx_note_content"><sup class="ltx_note_mark">2</sup>
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_note">2</span>
            
            
            
            
            
            
            
          <a href="https://github.com/adobe-research/custom-diffusion" title="" class="ltx_ref ltx_url ltx_font_typewriter">https://github.com/adobe-research/custom-diffusion</a></span></span></span>. We train each setting with a learning rate of <math id="S1a.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1\times 10^{-4}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1\times 10^{-4}</annotation></semantics></math>, step size of <math id="S1a.p4.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="500\times" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>500</mn><mo lspace="0.222em">×</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">500\times</annotation></semantics></math> number of subjects, and batch size of 1. Generated images shown in our paper were trained with prior preservation loss that prevents the leak of personalized concepts when generating other concepts in diffusion models. Loss weight of 1 was used for prior preservation loss. 200 class images were used for prior preservation loss.</p>
</div>
<div id="S1a.p5" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S1a.p5.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S1a.p5.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Cones2 <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib21" title="" class="ltx_ref">21</a>]</cite>.</span>
We use the official implementation for Cones2<span id="footnote3" class="ltx_note ltx_role_footnote"><sup class="ltx_note_mark">3</sup><span class="ltx_note_outer"><span class="ltx_note_content"><sup class="ltx_note_mark">3</sup>
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_note">3</span>
            
            
            
            
            
            
            
          <a href="https://github.com/ali-vilab/Cones-V2" title="" class="ltx_ref ltx_url ltx_font_typewriter">https://github.com/ali-vilab/Cones-V2</a></span></span></span>. We train each setting with a learning rate of <math id="S1a.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1\times 10^{-4}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1\times 10^{-4}</annotation></semantics></math>, step size of 1500, and batch size of 1. With prompt regularization. We implement layout guidance for inference 2 objects and 3 objects.</p>
</div>
<div id="S1a.p6" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S1a.p6.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S1a.p6.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">EDLoRA <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib9" title="" class="ltx_ref">9</a>]</cite>.</span>
We use the official implementation for EDLoRA<span id="footnote4" class="ltx_note ltx_role_footnote"><sup class="ltx_note_mark">4</sup><span class="ltx_note_outer"><span class="ltx_note_content"><sup class="ltx_note_mark">4</sup>
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_note">4</span>
            
            
            
            
            
            
            
          <a href="https://github.com/TencentARC/Mix-of-Show.git" title="" class="ltx_ref ltx_url ltx_font_typewriter">https://github.com/TencentARC/Mix-of-Show.git</a></span></span></span>. We implement this code to SD2.1 for comparison. We train each EDLoRA with setting with learning rate of <math id="S1a.p6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1\times 10^{-3}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1\times 10^{-3}</annotation></semantics></math> for text embedding, <math id="S1a.p6.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1\times 10^{-5}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>5</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1\times 10^{-5}</annotation></semantics></math> for text encoder and <math id="S1a.p6.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1\times 10^{-4}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1\times 10^{-4}</annotation></semantics></math> for unet. We set every rank of LoRA to 4. We set the alpha value for gradient fusion to 1 for the U-net and text encoder.</p>
</div>
<div id="S1a.p7" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S1a.p7.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S1a.p7.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">ConceptSplit (Ours)</span></p>
</div>
<div id="S1a.p8" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S1a.p8.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S1a.p8.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">ToVA.</span> We used LoRA with rank 64 for our ToVA, and we used prompt regularization, as proposed in Cones2 <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib21" title="" class="ltx_ref">21</a>]</cite> We utilized 200 prompts using ChatGPT <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib26" title="" class="ltx_ref">26</a>]</cite> and apply different prompt for each iteration. We trained with 300 iterations for our experiments. With a learning rate of 1e-4 and batch size of 1.</p>
</div>
<div id="S1a.p9" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S1a.p9.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S1a.p9.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">LODA.</span> We set LODA step <math id="S1a.p9.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>N</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N</annotation></semantics></math> to 10. with percent hyperparameter <math id="S1a.p9.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>γ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma</annotation></semantics></math> 0.9 and ReLU threshold <math id="S1a.p9.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>τ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau</annotation></semantics></math> to 1.0. We set each strength hyperparameter <math id="S1a.p9.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p,m" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p,m</annotation></semantics></math> to +5 and -1e8. Update rate <math id="S1a.p9.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\eta_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>η</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\eta_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> was scheduled linearly with <math id="S1a.p9.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="40-20\cdot\frac{t}{T}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>40</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>20</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mfrac><mi>t</mi><mi>T</mi></mfrac></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">40-20\cdot\frac{t}{T}</annotation></semantics></math>, where <math id="S1a.p9.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>T</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T</annotation></semantics></math> denotes the total steps.</p>
</div>
<figure id="S1.T2" class="ltx_table">
<div id="S1.T2.3" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_center ltx_transformed_outer" style="width:371.4pt;height:242.2pt;vertical-align:-119.1pt;"><span class="ltx_transformed_inner" style="transform:translate(-46.4pt,30.3pt) scale(0.8,0.8) ;">
